    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Chervil&nbsp;(</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=0d63aef30b57140a&amp;rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;cs=0&amp;sxsrf=AHTn8zp0eMr9EfYCytSZ2KeVqQjD6zdoPA%3A1745688423148&amp;q=Anthriscus+cerefolium&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwj8o8mSnPaMAxWBGzQIHQ4oHSkQxccNegQIBBAB&amp;mstk=AUtExfB_a8wF_AvlPi_37vnUSv7ie5_PGmHbZmO7VDDbj4YeZfzSn5v29M5F5EA2kiZzi8nTv4pRoOq6fugWbogONSOf6bNne2Sq3N7Yd5pcSYX5m8QzSl_iYl4_0D76MTvIIk1uZz4flrWdlbuVWK9gmZsr0-grMWNmMoz0kfhW5OC6g8bOf0UCRagoDFfh7dtS9C6r3szhjn-OEx-Rxe67KLqYsMayYJ7xVPf-Y4eW7B0iIWRHA1tEFZYimKcVb9LMCCavrO4sO0wl4_3veKhM9YlDDMMWOvIgiZUf8Yj7sS6cNw&amp;csui=3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Anthriscus cerefolium</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">)&nbsp;is a culinary herb known for its delicate, anise-flavored leaves, often compared to a milder version of parsley or tarragon.&nbsp;It's an annual or biennial herb, meaning it typically completes its life cycle in one or two years, respectively.&nbsp;Chervil is easy to grow, whether from seed or in containers.&nbsp;The plant produces&nbsp;small, white flowers in umbels (umbrella-like clusters) during midsummer, which attract pollinators.</span></p>",
